From the [specs](http://facebook.github.io/graphql/#sec-Errors)

> GraphQL servers may provide additional entries to error as they choose to produce more helpful or machine‐readable errors, however future versions of the spec may describe additional entries to errors.

As far as I understand, we should be able to define custom properties to errors that are being exposed to the GraphQL response. Like this:

```
{
  "errors": [
    {
      "message": "Name for character with ID 1002 could not be fetched.",
+    "type": "NOT_FOUND",
      "locations": [ { "line": 6, "column": 7 } ],
      "path": [ "hero", "heroFriends", 1, "name" ]
    }
  ],
  "data": {
    "hero": {
      "name": "R2-D2",
      "heroFriends": [
        {
          "id": "1000",
          "name": "Luke Skywalker"
        },
        null,
        {
          "id": "1003",
          "name": "Leia Organa"
        }
      ]
    }
  }
}
```

Is this currently possible? Should we consider adding it to this library?

Can we add somehow the name of a field which has an invalid value? I would like to use this inside `parseLiteral` - that's where I do validation and where the GraphQLError with a custom message is thrown.

```
mutation RootMutation {
  addUser(
    email: "invalid.email",
  ){email}
}
```

``` js
  return new GraphQLScalarType({
    name: attrs.name,
    serialize: function(value) {
      return value;
    },
    parseValue: function(value) {
      return value;
    },
    parseLiteral: function(ast) {
      if (!isValid) {
        throw new GraphQLError(`The field ${ast.fieldName} is invalid.`, [ast]); // HERE
      }
      return ast.value;
    }
  });
```

```
{
  "errors": [
    {
      "message": "\"Email\" is invalid.",
      "locations": [
        {
          "line": 5,
          "column": 12,
          "field": "email" // HERE
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
```

Hello everyone! I am missing a feature here that is about error output.

I really wish to send an Error Code alongside the error message, but I am not able to do this yet.

I wish I could do something like this:

``` js
const error = new Error('Permission Denied');
error.code = 403;

throw error;
```

and receive a response like this

``` json
{
  "data": {
    "user": {
      "email": null
    }
  },
  "errors": [
    {
      "code": 403,
      "message": "Permission Denied",
      "locations": [
        {
          "line": 1,
          "column": 3
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
```
